<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">draughts</ansi>

A mana draught gives back part of the drinker's mana at once. Mana doesn't
come back on its own (<ansi fg="command">help mana</ansi>), so a draught is how a caster keeps
going between rests.

  <ansi fg="yellow">minor mana draught</ansi>     25% of the drinker's maximum mana    50 gold
  <ansi fg="yellow">lesser mana draught</ansi>    40%                                  150 gold
  <ansi fg="yellow">greater mana draught</ansi>   60%                                  350 gold

Prices are what a shop asks. Moilyn, the wizard in Frostfang, sells the
minor and lesser draughts. No shop sells a greater draught. A wizard
starts with one minor draught.

A draught is drunk out of battle only, never during one:

  <ansi fg="command">drink minor mana draught</ansi>

A draught can't raise mana past the maximum.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help mana</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help drink</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help patch</ansi>.
